// The `pd`-frame route of `BUG-wQ9tL`: the compile-time gate fires for an
// initializer, and the *runtime* check has to be emitted too, keyed on the
// module that declared the `pd` (`util`) and not on `main`, whose frame the
// initializer runs in. The path is outside `util`'s grant, so this is denied
// with `util`'s own allowlist in the message.
impl "util" caps(fs = ["__KELP_SCRATCH__/kelp_caps_pd_gated_denied/**"])

fun main() {
    print(util.show())
}
